<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Taru is a full-stack web application that serves three distinct user roles, each with a dedicated portal, authentication flow, and dashboard. The platform is designed to be student-first while also empowering mental health professionals and educational institutions with the tools they need. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (Educational institutions get access to an admin dashboard with aggregate student analytics, visual mood trend charts across the student body, an enrolled student list with search and filtering capabilities, and check-in participation rate monitoring. This portal enables data-driven decisions for campus-wide wellbeing programs. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (A dedicated portal for mental health professionals includes its own registration and login system, a dashboard to manage upcoming appointments, tools to configure weekly availability slots, and the ability to conduct video consultations with students. During sessions, psychiatrists can view the student's mood history and use an in-meeting text chat panel for sharing resources. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (The primary interface for students provides a comprehensive suite of wellbeing tools. Students can perform daily check-ins that assess seven dimensions of emotional health \(mood, energy, stress, sleep, concentration, social support, and motivation\). The platform tracks check-in streaks to encourage consistent self-monitoring. Students can visualize mood trends through weekly charts and a calendar-based history view. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 86 0 R
/E (For support, students can connect through anonymous peer chat \(random matchmaking with auto-generated usernames\), an AI chatbot for 24/7 guidance, or by booking appointments with certified psychiatrists for WebRTC-based video consultations. Stress- relief features include a Breathing Bubble component and five multiplayer games designed to ground and calm the mind. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
