/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Keeping game state consistent across two players with variable network latency could lead to desynchronization. This was solved by adopting a server-authoritative model where all game logic and move validation runs on the server; clients receive only authoritative state updates and render accordingly. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 93 0 R
/E (Cross-origin issues arose when deploying the frontend and backend to different domains. This was resolved by simplifying the CORS configuration to accept an array of allowed origins from environment variables, enabling seamless deployment on Vercel. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
